Crush 80 per-key backlight
Copyright 2026 Adam Yung

led_map_data.h (generated by scripts/rgb/derive_led_map.py) carries the key-to-LED order of the Crush 80,
read from the stock firmware's switch-to-LED table by Ritwick Verma and published in
https://github.com/RitwickVerma/Crush80_ZMK (zmk/src/rainy_rgb/led_map.c), licensed Apache-2.0.
That fork builds on the WS2812 driver of scholzri (Rainy 75 ZMK), also Apache-2.0.
The table here is re-keyed by matrix position for this board's 86-key transform: a modified work.
The engine itself (engine.c) is original; its idea of reading the live keymap to colour keys follows the
same fork's Fn-layer overlay.
